# Theme Conventions

## 4 Theme Modes

```kotlin
enum class ThemeMode { LIGHT, DARK, ABYSS, SYSTEM }
```

- **LIGHT**: `MezonLightScheme` — white/gray surfaces
- **DARK**: `MezonDarkScheme` — dark gray surfaces (`#1C1D22`)
- **ABYSS**: `MezonAbyssScheme` — deep purple/navy (`#110B33`) — extends `darkColorScheme`
- **SYSTEM**: follows device dark/light setting

## ThemeManager (DataStore persistence)

```kotlin
@Singleton
class ThemeManager @Inject constructor(
    private val dataStore: DataStore<Preferences>
) {
    val themeMode: Flow<ThemeMode>
    suspend fun setTheme(mode: ThemeMode)
}
```

Located in `session/ThemeManager.kt`. Persists theme choice as string in DataStore.

## Color Organization

### Shared brand colors (top-level vals in `Color.kt`)

```kotlin
val Blurple = Color(0xFF5A62F4)     // Primary brand color
val LinkBlue = Color(0xFF3297FF)    // Tertiary / links
val MezonRed = Color(0xFFD30E0E)    // Error
val MezonGreen = Color(0xFF00D4AA)  // Online indicator
val SuccessGreen = Color(0xFF16A34A)
```

### Theme-specific palettes (objects in `Color.kt`)

```kotlin
object MezonDarkColors { val Primary, Secondary, Tertiary, Border, Text, TextStrong, ... }
object MezonAbyssColors { val Primary, Secondary, SecondaryWeight, ... }
object MezonLightColors { val Primary, Secondary, Tertiary, Border, Text, TextStrong, ... }
```

### Rules

- NEVER use raw `Color(0xFF...)` in composables — always use `MaterialTheme.colorScheme.*`
- Brand colors (`Blurple`, `LinkBlue`, `MezonRed`) may be used directly since they are theme-independent
- Each theme scheme must map ALL Material3 `ColorScheme` slots — no defaults
- Abyss theme reuses `MezonDarkColors.Text*` for text — this is intentional (consistent readability across dark variants)
- Color constants are ALWAYS top-level vals or object properties — never created inside composition

## XML Window Background

Two XML theme files prevent flash during Activity recreation:

- `values/themes.xml`: `windowBackground = #FFF2F3F5` (matches `MezonLightColors.Primary`)
- `values-night/themes.xml`: `windowBackground = #FF1C1D22` (matches `MezonDarkColors.Primary`)

Known limitation: Abyss theme will flash Dark background on Activity recreation since XML can't detect Compose theme mode.

## MezonTheme Composable

```kotlin
@Composable
fun MezonTheme(themeMode: ThemeMode = ThemeMode.SYSTEM, content: @Composable () -> Unit) {
    val colorScheme = when (themeMode) { ... }
    val dimens = rememberScreenDimens()
    val typography = scaledTypography(dimens)

    CompositionLocalProvider(
        LocalDimens provides dimens,
        LocalThemeMode provides themeMode
    ) {
        MaterialTheme(colorScheme = colorScheme, typography = typography, content = content)
    }
}
```

Theme integrates responsive typography via `scaledTypography(dimens)`.

## Adding a New Theme

1. Define color palette object in `Color.kt`
2. Create `ColorScheme` in `Theme.kt` using `darkColorScheme()` or `lightColorScheme()`
3. Add enum value to `ThemeMode`
4. Add case to `when (themeMode)` in `MezonTheme`
5. Add DataStore string mapping in `ThemeManager`
6. If dark variant: XML `windowBackground` will show Dark theme colors on recreation (acceptable)
